.TH ZWM 1 "June 2026" "1.0" "ZWM Manual"
.SH NAME
zwm \- minimal X11 tiling window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zwm
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zwm
is a minimal and opinionated tiling window manager for X11.
It uses XCB for communication with the X server and manages tiled windows with
a customized binary space partitioning tree.
.PP
ZWM supports keyboard-driven window management, mouse-assisted movement and
resizing, EWMH integration for panels, configurable window rules, multiple
virtual desktops, hot configuration reloads, and the default, master, stack,
grid, monocle, three-column, and deck layouts.
.SH OPTIONS
ZWM currently takes no command-line options.
.SH CONFIGURATION
On first run, ZWM creates a configuration file at:
.PP
.RS
.B ~/.config/zwm/zwm.conf
.RE
.PP
The installed template is normally located at:
.PP
.RS
.B /usr/share/zwm/zwm.conf
.RE
.SS Startup commands
Run a command when ZWM starts:
.PP
.nf
exec = "polybar"
exec = ["polybar", "-c", ".config/polybar/config.ini"]
.fi
.SS Variables
The default configuration uses these variables:
.PP
.nf
border_width = 2
active_border_color = 0x4a4a48
normal_border_color = 0x30302f
window_gap = 10
virtual_desktops = 7
focus_follow_pointer = true
focus_follow_spawn = false
restore_last_focus = false
.fi
.TP
.B border_width
Width of the focused and unfocused window border in pixels.
.TP
.B active_border_color
Focused window border color, written as a hexadecimal RGB value.
.TP
.B normal_border_color
Unfocused window border color, written as a hexadecimal RGB value.
.TP
.B window_gap
Gap between tiled windows in pixels.
.TP
.B virtual_desktops
Number of virtual desktops.
.TP
.B focus_follow_pointer
When true, focus follows pointer enter events. When false, windows are focused
by click or key actions.
.TP
.B focus_follow_spawn
When true, newly spawned windows automatically receive focus.
.TP
.B restore_last_focus
When true, ZWM restores the previously focused window when switching desktops
if the target desktop layout is not stack.
.SS Window rules
Window rules match a window class and set the initial window state and desktop.
Use
.BR xprop (1)
to inspect a window's class.
.PP
.nf
rule = wm_class("window class name"), state(tiled|floated), desktop(1..N)
rule = wm_class("firefox"), state(tiled), desktop(-1)
.fi
.PP
Use
.B desktop(-1)
to leave the window on its current desktop.
.SS Key binding syntax
Key bindings use this form:
.PP
.nf
bind = modifier + key -> action
.fi
.PP
Two modifiers are combined with a pipe:
.PP
.nf
bind = super|shift + c -> func(layout:grid)
.fi
.PP
Supported modifiers are
.BR super ,
.BR alt ,
.BR shift ,
and
.BR ctrl .
Supported key names are
.BR 0-9 ,
.BR a-z ,
.BR space ,
.BR return ,
.BR left ,
.BR up ,
.BR right ,
and
.BR down .
.SS Actions
.TP
.B run(...)
Execute a program. A single string runs one command; a list passes arguments.
.TP
.B func(kill)
Kill or close the focused window.
.TP
.B func(switch_desktop:N)
Switch to desktop
.IR N .
.TP
.B func(resize:grow|shrink)
Grow or shrink the focused tiled split, or the main split in deck and
three-column layouts.
.TP
.B func(fullscreen)
Toggle fullscreen for the focused window.
.TP
.B func(swap)
Swap the focused window with its sibling.
.TP
.B func(cycle_window:up|right|left|down)
Move focus in the requested direction.
.TP
.B func(cycle_monitors:next|prev)
Move focus between monitors.
.TP
.B func(shift_window:up|right|left|down)
Move a floating window by 10 pixels.
.TP
.B func(grow_floating_window:horizontal|vertical)
Grow a floating window on the requested axis.
.TP
.B func(shrink_floating_window:horizontal|vertical)
Shrink a floating window on the requested axis.
.TP
.B func(change_state:tile|float)
Set the focused window to tiled or floating state.
.TP
.B func(cycle_desktop:left|right)
Cycle through virtual desktops.
.TP
.B func(transfer_node:N)
Move the focused window to desktop
.IR N .
.TP
.B func(layout:master|stack|default|grid|monocle|three_col|deck)
Switch the current desktop layout.
.TP
.B func(traverse:up|down)
Traverse windows in stack, monocle, or deck layouts.
.TP
.B func(flip)
Flip the focused window or partition orientation.
.TP
.B func(start_keyboard_drag)
Enter keyboard-driven drag mode for tiled windows.
.TP
.B func(reload_config)
Reload the configuration file without restarting ZWM.
